      "description": "Watch Galatasaray vs Kocaelispor highlights and goals from Süper Lig on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 13, 2026. The Süper Lig delivered a captivating encounter as Galatasaray hosted Kocaelispor in a match defined by tactical patience and defensive resilience. Both sides entered the pitch looking to claim dominance in a clash that kept fans on the edge of their seats until the final whistle. A Tactical Stalemate in the Opening Period Kicking off on September 13, 2026 , the match began with high energy and physical duels across the pitch. Galatasaray looked to establish control early on, but Kocaelispor proved to be a tough nut to crack, maintaining a compact shape. The intensity of the contest was highlighted in the 22nd minute when Anfernee Dijksteel picked up a yellow card for a robust challenge. Despite several probes into the final third, neither side could find the clinical touch required to break the deadlock before the halftime whistle blew after three minutes of added time. Batrakov and Bardakcı Break the Resistance The second half saw an increase in urgency from the home side. After Deniz Gul received a caution in the 56th minute, the game reached its turning point with a double substitution in the 59th minute, most notably bringing on Aleksey Batrakov for Gabriel Sara . The impact was almost immediate; in the 71st minute, Batrakov turned provider, delivering a perfect ball for Abdulkerim Bardakcı to head home the opening goal. The goalscorer was booked shortly after in the 72nd minute as emotions ran high in the stadium. Holding Firm in the Closing Stages As the match entered its final phase, both managers utilized their benches to influence the outcome. Kocaelispor introduced fresh energy with the likes of Metehan Altunbas , while Galatasaray looked to solidify their lead by bringing on Leroy Sane and Ismail Jakobs . The closing minutes were a test of nerves for the hosts, further emphasized by a late yellow card for Roland Sallai in the 94th minute. However, the defense held strong through the final moments of stoppage time, ensuring that all three points remained at home in this hard-fought Süper Lig fixture."
